ed in the 13th century when it was just a fishing village; however, it became much more important after World War I when it was rebuilt completely from scratch as a planned city, filled with modernist architecture, military harbour and seaport which served newly independent Poland. It remains one of the most important coastal cities in Poland with large cargo traffic and a navy base. In 2026, the city centre was designated as a UNESCO World Heritage Site.","grounding":[{"source":"wikivoyage","title":"Gdynia","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Gdynia","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"short":"Gdynia is a modern port in northern Poland, part of the Tricity alongside Gdansk and Sopot. The tall ship Dar Pomorza is moored on the waterfront, Sea Towers rises behind it, and ten hours covers the city. June to August is the season.","short_src":"rewrite","facts":{"population":257000,"visit_h":9.6}},"highlights":[{"id":"hl-orp-blyskawica","name":"ORP Błyskawica","kind":"Museum","lat":54.51955,"lon":18.55121,"dist_km":1.2,"rank_score":9.2,"resolved_by":"catalogue"},{"id":"hl-stadion-miejski","name":"Stadion Miejski","kind":"Landmark","lat":54.49314,"lon":18.53121,"dist_km":2.9,"rank_score":6.85,"resolved_by":"catalogue","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Stadion_miejski_w_Gdyni.jpg/960px-Stadion_miejski_w_Gdyni.jpg","author":"Mariusz Nasieniewski","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stadion_miejski_w_Gdyni.jpg","w":4000,"h":2650,"ok_print":true}},{"id":"hl-forest-opera","name":"Forest Opera","kind":"Theatre","lat":54.4448,"lon":18.5444,"dist_km":8.3,"rank_score":6.7,"resolved_by":"catalogue","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Sopot_-_Opera_Le%C5%9Bna_%283%29.JPG/960px-Sopot_-_Opera_Le%C5%9Bna_%283%29.JPG","author":"Gdaniec","licence":"CC BY 3.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0",